      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix: load plan utilization history off the startup main thread",
        "body": "## Problem\n\n`UsageStore.init` synchronously decoded persisted plan-utilization history on the main actor. Mature histories could therefore hold the app's startup path before AppKit entered its normal run loop.\n\n## Fix\n\n- Own the utility-priority decode worker directly so cancellation covers the gate, disk read, decode, and publication path.\n- Gate history readers and mutations until the one-shot load completes, preventing an initial refresh from overwriting persisted samples.\n- Make gated cancellation waiter-specific and prove the suspended worker drains without publishing.\n- Preserve synchronous seeded-history fixtures while keeping ordinary test startup free of automatic background work and production history directories.\n- Serialize/coalesce persistence and add a deterministic drain seam for merge-and-save regression coverage.\n- Keep persistence schema, retention, account ownership, sampling, and chart behavior unchanged.\n\n## Verification\n\nExact PR head: `170e17718af79f0f609a5a8350224a3ef5961716` (tree `a7c8f86be3abd2e66f4ba9349993f78cae3e6115`). Its source tree is byte-identical to signed candidate `fca0226fa2b1a248a5a3bbf10bdb2aadb8126715`; the merge commit only preserves the contributor's concurrent branch update without a destructive force-push.\n\n- `make check`: clean; SwiftLint reported 0 violations across 1,421 files.\n- `make test`: 633/633 selections in 53/53 groups, all first-pass green; zero retries or timeouts.\n- `swift test --filter UsageStorePlanUtilizationAsyncLoadTests`: 10/10 passed.\n- Focused plan-utilization, hosted-submenu, closed-menu, and account-menu regression suites passed.\n- Structured autoreview of every maintainer repair bundle: no accepted/actionable findings.\n\nSigned live startup proof on macOS Tahoe 26.5 used identical valid 41 MiB histories (438,000 entries) and three fresh isolated launches per build:\n\n- Baseline `430c2401`: history JSON decode occupied the main thread for 759 / 728 / 734 one-millisecond samples.\n- Signed candidate tree (`fca0226f`, identical to exact PR head `170e1771`): 0 / 0 / 0 main-thread decode samples; decode ran on the utility cooperative queue for 636 / 783 / 705 samples while the main thread was already in the normal `NSApplication` run loop.\n- Both bundles passed strict deep code-sign verification and Gatekeeper with Developer ID team `Y5PE65HELJ`.\n- Fixture hashes were unchanged before/after every run, all tested processes exited, and source-blind validation passed all 6 contract clauses.\n- Exact-head proof archive SHA-256: `0e366d9962e10d6fed5435539ca4a59dafbe1e0271e676b1d9251a8abd2f1fcc`.\n\nThe Tahoe beta's App Launch trace template kernel-panicked in `kernelmanagerd`, so the successful proof used pre-armed one-millisecond `sample` traces against the exact directly launched binaries instead. No screenshots or credentials were used.\n",
